+namespace helium {
+
+// helium-fork: how far outside the panel its shadow spreads -- the room a
+// caller has to reserve around the panel rect, whether that is a popup widget's
+// bounds or a view's. Positive insets, the way
+// views::BubbleBorder::GetBorderAndShadowInsets() reports them.
+gfx::Insets ArcOmniboxPanelShadowInsets(const ArcOmniboxPanelMetrics& metrics);
+
+// helium-fork: paints the Arc shell's edit-state panel -- `panel` filled with
+// `background` at the metrics' radius, lifted off what is behind it by Dia's
+// shadow.
+//
+// Two callers, one painter, on purpose: the omnibox popup's frame draws it
+// when there are suggestions and ArcOmniboxPanelView draws it when the field is
+// focused with none, and the user must not be able to tell which one is on
+// screen. Anything either of them wants to do differently belongs in the
+// arguments, not in a second copy of this.
+//
+// `hole`, when given, is the address field's rect: it is clipped away so the
+// real field shows through the panel rather than being painted over. Only the
+// focus-panel caller needs it -- the popup covers the field with its own
+// opaque layer and cuts its hole inside that.
+//
+// Why a draw looper rather than ui::Shadow, which is what the content card
+// uses: ui::Shadow caps elevation at `(min(w, h) - 2 * radius) / 4`, and the
+// panel is 31pt tall with a 14pt radius before any suggestions arrive -- that
+// caps to zero and the shadow simply never appears. The looper has no such
+// coupling, and using it in both states is also what keeps the two identical
+// at the moment the popup opens.
+//
+// `dark` selects between the metrics' two alpha pairs; it is the theme's own
+// notion of darkness, not the page's -- the panel is a chrome surface and does
+// not follow the band's page tint.
+void PaintArcOmniboxPanel(gfx::Canvas* canvas,
+                          const ArcOmniboxPanelMetrics& metrics,
+                          const gfx::Rect& panel,
+                          SkColor background,
+                          bool dark,
+                          std::optional<gfx::Rect> hole = std::nullopt);
+
+}  // namespace helium
+
+#endif  // CHROME_BROWSER_UI_VIEWS_HELIUM_ARC_OMNIBOX_PANEL_PAINTER_H_
